(Bug #79 is about a top-level READ above the variable's own declaration.
 A write is a different statement and is deliberately left alone: the
 order it describes is well defined - store 9, then the declaration
 stores 5 - and nothing reads a slot nobody has written. This pins that
 the fix did not widen into `Set`, and pins the answer the order gives.)

Set tally to 9.
a number called tally is 5.
Print tally.

Set tally to 12.
Print tally.
